  "goodToKnow": "Der Bundesstaat has two meanings: a federal state as a type (Deutschland, Österreich and die Schweiz sind Bundesstaaten) and a member state of a federation, such as the US states or Indian states. For Germany's sixteen member states, German uses das Bundesland or simply das Land (plural Länder). In Switzerland, the member states are Kantone. So California is ein US-Bundesstaat, while Bavaria is ein Bundesland."
